Third-party components
----------------------

These parts are not covered by the terms above and keep their own licenses:

- tools/builder/third_party/miniz.c, miniz.h: MIT, see tools/builder/third_party/miniz-LICENSE.
- tools/builder/third_party/stb_image.h, stb_image_write.h, stb_truetype.h, stb_vorbis.c: MIT or public domain, see
  the end of each file.
- web/vendor/fflate.js: MIT, see web/vendor/fflate-LICENSE.
- engine/third_party/tremor: the Tremor Vorbis decoder, BSD, (c) Xiph.Org Foundation, see
  engine/third_party/tremor/COPYING.
- engine/third_party/stb_image_write.h: MIT or public domain, see the end of the file.
- tools/builder/art/psp.svg: based on "PSP 2000 Black" by Todd Partridge (Gen2ly), Openclipart, CC0.
- .github/controls: the PSP-2000 by Todd Partridge, the 3DS by BHSPitMonkey and the Wii Remote by lexaficus are from
  Openclipart (CC0); the PS3, GameCube and Xbox 360 controllers are by Grumbel (CC0), and the PS2 controller is
  adapted from that PS3 drawing. The PS Vita and Wii U GamePad drawings are by Tokyoship on Wikimedia Commons, CC BY
  3.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/), with the Vita recolored white for the dark theme.
- The CIA template embedded in the builder is made at build time with makerom (Project_CTR, (c) 3DSGuy, MIT) and
  bannertool ((c) Steveice10 and carstene1ns, MIT). Neither tool is included in this repository.
- The PS2 engine is linked with ps2sdk (Academic Free License 2.0, (c) the ps2dev contributors) and embeds its IOP
  modules iomanX, fileXio, libsd, audsrv, usbd, bdm, bdmfs_fatfs and usbmass_bd. It also links libvorbis and libogg
  (BSD, (c) Xiph.Org Foundation) and zlib (zlib license, (c) Jean-loup Gailly and Mark Adler) from ps2sdk-ports.
  None of them are included in this repository; they come with the ps2dev toolchain.
- The PS3 engine is linked with PSL1GHT (MIT, (c) the PSL1GHT contributors). It also links libvorbis and libogg
  (BSD, (c) Xiph.Org Foundation) and zlib (zlib license, (c) Jean-loup Gailly and Mark Adler). None of them are
  included in this repository; scripts/setup-ps3dev.sh downloads and builds them into _deps.
- The RPG Maker MV runtime logic in engine/src/game is ported from the RPG Maker MV corescript, used under the
  following license:

